## Description
Added simple WebSocket reload functionality that refreshes connected clients when file changes are detected and processed. This includes server initialization, client connection handling, and reload event implementation.

## Related Issue(s)
- Closes #[ISSUE_NUMBER] (WebSocket Reload Event)

## Type of Change
- [x] ✨ New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)
- [x] 🔧 Build configuration update

## Changes Made
1. Added WebSocket server configuration with dynamic port
2. Implemented client connection handling in server
3. Added WebSocket instance to global configuration
4. Implemented client-side WebSocket connection and reload handler
5. Added reload event trigger after successful file upload
6. Updated type definitions for WebSocket support

### Key Changes:

#### Server Configuration:
```typescript
// Added WebSocket server initialization with port
const websocketServer = new WebSocketServer({
  port: 8080, // TODO: Generate a port number
});

// Handle client connections
websocketServer.on('connection', (ws) => {
  globalThis.config.ws = ws;
});
```

#### Client-Side Implementation:
```javascript
// Added client-side WebSocket initialization and reload handler
window.FrameworkServer = ${JSON.stringify(globalThis.config.websocketServer.address())}

class FrameworkOverlay extends HTMLElement {
  constructor() {
    super();
    // ... existing code ...
    this.ws.onmessage = (event) => {
      if (event.data === 'reload') {
        window.location.reload();
      }
      console.log(event);
    };
  }
}
```

#### Upload Handler:
```typescript
// Added reload trigger after successful upload
await globalThis.config.shopifyClient.uploadFile(sanitizedPath, uploadContent);
globalThis.config.ws.send('reload');
LogSuccess(`Processed, compiled, and uploaded: ${sanitizedPath}`);
```

#### Type Definitions:
```typescript
// Updated global config types
export interface GlobalConfig {
  // ... existing types ...
  websocketServer: WebSocketServer;
  ws: WebSocket;
  port: number;
  vitePort: number;
  viteServerUrl: string;
}
```

