- The WebSocket port is currently hardcoded (8080) and should be made configurable in a future update
- WebSocket server is initialized once per Framework instance
- Reload events are sent immediately after successful file uploads
- Client maintains connection throughout development session

Adds methods for contraction hierarchy building. Does not include the shortest path algorithm.

- Adds two columns to the query result: vertex_order, metric, the first one giving an order of the vertices by increasing values of the metric. PgTap tests are adapted consequently;
- Makes a few homogeneization of code between the three methods (in particular the `process_shortcut` method);
- PgTap tests are added for the contractions hierarchy method, on a specific toy graph;
- The new method is documented, using the main sample graph as an example, in order to be consistent with the former documentation of the two first contraction methods.
Remark: it is clearly not the most adapted to the Contractions Hierarchies Method, an improvement could be to find a graph which makes sense for the three contraction methods.

